# token-harness local corpus (BY PATH ONLY -- never copy PDFs into the repo).
#
# Copy this file to `scripts/token-harness.corpus` (which is gitignored) and
# list one absolute-or-relative PATH to a local PDF per line. The harness reads
# these paths, converts them, and reports the same metrics as for the synthetic
# fixtures. Paths that do not exist are skipped silently, so it is safe to keep
# machine-specific entries here.
#
# Per kopitiam_token_max.md §2.4, these copyrighted papers live OUTSIDE the
# repo. Only their measurements (numbers) ever appear in harness output, never
# their content, and output uses the basename only -- no absolute paths leak.
#
# You can also pass paths at runtime without a file:
#   KOPITIAM_TOKEN_CORPUS="/papers/a.pdf;/papers/b.pdf" scripts/token-harness.sh
#
# Example entries (delete these; they are illustrative):
# C:/Users/me/papers/proceedings-volume.pdf
# /home/me/papers/diagram-heavy-chapter.pdf
